0..67 Comment "// A case that prunes: an arm whose constructor cannot stand at the"
68..144 Comment "// scrutinee\'s index is left out. Each branch of a case on an indexed family"
145..221 Comment "// binds, past its fields, the path from the index its constructor states to"
222..298 Comment "// the scrutinee\'s; a left-out arm eliminates that path, its two ends apart,"
299..369 Comment "// which needs no rule beyond the case of no arms (Cockx, Devriese and"
370..447 Comment "// Piessens, _Unifiers as equivalences_, doi:10.1145/2951913.2951917). An arm"
448..523 Comment "// whose ends are not apart cannot be left out; that is in the pathological"
524..532 Comment "// twin."
534..571 Comment "// The naturals the lengths count in."
